<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea plans to supply 800 bln won to banks.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea plans to supply 800 bln won to banks.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea plans to supply 800 billion won to the banking system on Thursday through eight-day repurchase agreements, an official at the bank said.  </p>
<p>He said the planned fund supply was aimed at helping ease shortages in daily won reserve levels at several banks.</p>
<p>An auction is due to be held in the afternoon for the fund supply, he said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
